From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: OddBlueDog <3959851+OddBlueDog@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 12:56:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: no rx_lock when there are no frames to pass on

mt76_rx_complete() took dev->rx_lock even with no frames to pass on: after every NAPI poll of a ring that carries only events (tx-free, TX status), and after a reorder timeout that releases nothing. It returns at once now when there are none.

No test of its own: nothing changes for frames, and mt76-core-rx passes frames through it.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 mac80211.c | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/mac80211.c b/mac80211.c
index be4d0560..a858de2b 100644
--- a/mac80211.c
+++ b/mac80211.c
@@ -1657,6 +1657,10 @@ void mt76_rx_complete(struct mt76_dev *dev, struct sk_buff_head *frames,
 	struct sk_buff *skb, *tmp;
 	LIST_HEAD(list);
 
+	/* a tx-free or other event-only poll: no frames, no rx_lock */
+	if (skb_queue_empty(frames))
+		return;
+
 	spin_lock(&dev->rx_lock);
 	while ((skb = __skb_dequeue(frames)) != NULL) {
 		struct sk_buff *nskb = skb_shinfo(skb)->frag_list;
